-- Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2024 (Vic), S.R. No. 35/2024, version 001
-- (version as at 26 May 2024), read with the provisions of the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation
-- Act 2013 that they complete.
-- Seat: the worker (the injured worker, or a contractor deemed to be a worker).
-- Copyright (c) State of Victoria; Victorian Legislation, Office of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, with the authority
-- of the Government Printer. UNOFFICIAL: a Legalese Commons encoding of a plain-text conversion of the register's
-- Word file; only the authorised version is evidence (Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 s 64).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wirc-regs-dates`

§ `The worker's questions under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2024`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 8 — full-time worker (2013 Act s 3)`
-- s 3: "full-time worker means a worker who is employed for at least the normal number of hours fixed in any
-- industrial award applicable to the worker or, if there is no applicable award, the prescribed number of hours".
-- reg 8: "the prescribed number of hours is 35 hours each week".

`the prescribed hours for a full-time worker` MEANS 35

-- A "means" definition: FALSE is the text's own no.
@export Am I a full-time worker under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic), using the 35 hours a week the Regulations prescribe where no industrial award applies to me?
GIVEN `an industrial award applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an industrial award apply to your work for this employer? (yes or no)
      `the award's normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc If an award applies, the normal number of hours a week it fixes for your work (ignored if no award applies)
      `my weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week you are employed for by this employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I a full-time worker` MEANS
    IF `an industrial award applies to me`
    THEN `my weekly hours` AT LEAST `the award's normal weekly hours`
    ELSE `my weekly hours` AT LEAST `the prescribed hours for a full-time worker`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 9 — pre-injury average weekly earnings of a worker with two or more employers (2013 Act Sch 2 items 2-8)`
-- Situation: this group only arises if you had two or more employers when you were injured.
-- reg 9: for items 3, 5, 6 and 8 of Schedule 2 "the prescribed number of hours is 38 hours each week".
-- The same regulation sets the hours for items 3, 5, 6 and 8 of Schedule 1A to the Accident Compensation Act 1985;
-- that Act is not encoded here.

`the prescribed hours for pre-injury average weekly earnings` MEANS 38

-- One of the worker's employments at the time of injury.
DECLARE `Employment` HAS
    `award applies`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- an industrial award is applicable to this work
    `award ordinary hours` IS A NUMBER    -- the ordinary hours a week the award fixes (unused if none)
    `weekly hours`         IS A NUMBER    -- the hours a week worked for this employer (ordinary hours)
    `weekly earnings`      IS A NUMBER    -- ordinary earnings a week from this employer, in dollars

GIVEN `e` IS AN `Employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`works at least the award's ordinary hours in` `e` MEANS
    `e`'s `award applies` AND `e`'s `weekly hours` AT LEAST `e`'s `award ordinary hours`

GIVEN `e` IS AN `Employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`works at least the prescribed hours in` `e` MEANS
    `e`'s `weekly hours` AT LEAST `the prescribed hours for pre-injury average weekly earnings`

-- "to whom no industrial award is applicable" (items 3 and 6) is read of the worker: no award applies to any of the
-- employments. Fork F2 in NOTES.md gives the other reading (no award applies to the employment that meets the hours).
GIVEN `first` IS AN `Employment`, `second` IS AN `Employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no industrial award applies to the worker in` `first` `or` `second` MEANS
    (NOT (`first`'s `award applies`)) AND (NOT (`second`'s `award applies`))

-- A list helper: the item number in front of the rest, if its class fits.
GIVEN `the item` IS A NUMBER, `it fits` IS A BOOLEAN, `the rest` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`put` `the item` `first if` `it fits` `the rest` MEANS
    IF `it fits` THEN `the item` FOLLOWED BY `the rest` ELSE `the rest`

-- Items 2 to 7 of Schedule 2 whose class (column 2) fits; item 8 is "circumstances other than those described in the
-- preceding provisions". The items overlap; all that fit are returned, in the Schedule's order (fork F1).
GIVEN `first` IS AN `Employment`, `second` IS AN `Employment`,
      `incapacity for some employers only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Schedule 2 items for` `first` `and` `second` `incapacity` `incapacity for some employers only` MEANS
    IF `the found items` EQUALS EMPTY THEN LIST 8 ELSE `the found items`
    WHERE
        `item 2 fits` MEANS
                `works at least the award's ordinary hours in` `first`
            OR  `works at least the award's ordinary hours in` `second`
        `item 3 fits` MEANS
                (   `works at least the prescribed hours in` `first`
                 OR `works at least the prescribed hours in` `second`)
            AND `no industrial award applies to the worker in` `first` `or` `second`
        `item 4 fits` MEANS
                `works at least the award's ordinary hours in` `first`
            AND `works at least the award's ordinary hours in` `second`
        `item 5 fits` MEANS
                (   `works at least the award's ordinary hours in` `first`
                 AND `works at least the prescribed hours in` `second`)
            OR  (   `works at least the award's ordinary hours in` `second`
                 AND `works at least the prescribed hours in` `first`)
        `item 6 fits` MEANS
                `works at least the prescribed hours in` `first`
            AND `works at least the prescribed hours in` `second`
            AND `no industrial award applies to the worker in` `first` `or` `second`
        `item 7 fits` MEANS `incapacity for some employers only`
        `the found items` MEANS
            `put` 2 `first if` `item 2 fits`
              (`put` 3 `first if` `item 3 fits`
                (`put` 4 `first if` `item 4 fits`
                  (`put` 5 `first if` `item 5 fits`
                    (`put` 6 `first if` `item 6 fits`
                      (`put` 7 `first if` `item 7 fits` EMPTY)))))

-- Item 8, column 3: average ordinary earnings per hour for all work for all employers, multiplied by the lesser of
-- (a) the prescribed 38 hours a week and (b) the total of the worker's ordinary hours a week.
GIVEN `first` IS AN `Employment`, `second` IS AN `Employment`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the item 8 earnings for` `first` `and` `second` MEANS
    IF `the total hours` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the hourly rate` TIMES `the hours multiplier`)
    WHERE
        `the total hours` MEANS `first`'s `weekly hours` PLUS `second`'s `weekly hours`
        `the total earnings` MEANS `first`'s `weekly earnings` PLUS `second`'s `weekly earnings`
        `the hourly rate` MEANS `the total earnings` DIVIDED BY `the total hours`
        `the hours multiplier` MEANS
            IF `the prescribed hours for pre-injury average weekly earnings` LESS THAN `the total hours`
            THEN `the prescribed hours for pre-injury average weekly earnings`
            ELSE `the total hours`

GIVEN `award applies 1` IS A BOOLEAN, `award hours 1` IS A NUMBER, `hours 1` IS A NUMBER, `earnings 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Employment`
`the employment from` `award applies 1` `award hours 1` `hours 1` `earnings 1` MEANS
    `Employment` WITH
        `award applies`        IS `award applies 1`
        `award ordinary hours` IS `award hours 1`
        `weekly hours`         IS `hours 1`
        `weekly earnings`      IS `earnings 1`

@export If I had two employers when I was injured, which items of Schedule 2 to the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) describe me, for working out my pre-injury average weekly earnings (with the 38 hours a week the Regulations prescribe)?
GIVEN `an award applies in my first job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an industrial award apply to your work for your first employer? (yes or no)
      `the award's ordinary hours in my first job` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the ordinary hours a week that award fixes (ignored if no award applies)
      `my weekly hours in my first job` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary hours a week for your first employer when you were injured
      `an award applies in my second job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an industrial award apply to your work for your second employer? (yes or no)
      `the award's ordinary hours in my second job` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the ordinary hours a week that award fixes (ignored if no award applies)
      `my weekly hours in my second job` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary hours a week for your second employer when you were injured
      `my injury stops me working for one employer but not the other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your injury leave you unable to work for one or more of your employers, but not for all of them? (yes or no)
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Which items of Schedule 2 describe me` MEANS
    `the Schedule 2 items for`
        (`the employment from` `an award applies in my first job` `the award's ordinary hours in my first job` `my weekly hours in my first job` 0)
        `and`
        (`the employment from` `an award applies in my second job` `the award's ordinary hours in my second job` `my weekly hours in my second job` 0)
        `incapacity` `my injury stops me working for one employer but not the other`
    -- weekly earnings take the placeholder 0: no class test in items 2 to 7 reads them.

@export If I had two employers when I was injured and item 8 of Schedule 2 to the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) applies to me, what are my pre-injury average weekly earnings, with the 38 hours a week the Regulations prescribe? (No answer if another item applies: those use Division 1 of Part 5, not encoded here.)
GIVEN `an award applies in my first job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an industrial award apply to your work for your first employer? (yes or no)
      `the award's ordinary hours in my first job` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the ordinary hours a week that award fixes (ignored if no award applies)
      `my weekly hours in my first job` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary hours a week for your first employer when you were injured
      `my weekly earnings in my first job` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average ordinary earnings a week from your first employer, in dollars
      `an award applies in my second job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an industrial award apply to your work for your second employer? (yes or no)
      `the award's ordinary hours in my second job` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the ordinary hours a week that award fixes (ignored if no award applies)
      `my weekly hours in my second job` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary hours a week for your second employer when you were injured
      `my weekly earnings in my second job` IS A NUMBER @desc Your average ordinary earnings a week from your second employer, in dollars
      `my injury stops me working for one employer but not the other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your injury leave you unable to work for one or more of your employers, but not for all of them? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings under item 8` MEANS
    IF `the items` EQUALS (LIST 8)
    THEN `the item 8 earnings for` `the first employment` `and` `the second employment`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the first employment` MEANS
            `the employment from` `an award applies in my first job` `the award's ordinary hours in my first job` `my weekly hours in my first job` `my weekly earnings in my first job`
        `the second employment` MEANS
            `the employment from` `an award applies in my second job` `the award's ordinary hours in my second job` `my weekly hours in my second job` `my weekly earnings in my second job`
        `the items` MEANS
            `the Schedule 2 items for` `the first employment` `and` `the second employment` `incapacity` `my injury stops me working for one employer but not the other`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 10 — timber contractors: amounts that are not remuneration (2013 Act Sch 1 cl 6(3))`
-- Situation: this group only arises if you are a timber contractor deemed to be a worker under clause 6.
-- cl 6(3): "the amount payable by the principal to the timber contractor, less the applicable prescribed percentage
-- (if any), is deemed to be remuneration". reg 10: 25 per cent, where (a) the amount payable includes an amount for
-- materials or equipment required for the work, and (b) the contractor (i) purchases, or has purchased, them, or
-- (ii) provides their own.

`the timber contractor percentage` MEANS 25%

GIVEN `includes materials` IS A BOOLEAN, `purchases materials` IS A BOOLEAN, `provides own materials` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the materials circumstances hold` `includes materials` `purchases materials` `provides own materials` MEANS
        `includes materials`
    AND (`purchases materials` OR `provides own materials`)

-- Deemed remuneration is NOTHING when the contractor is not deemed a worker: clause 6(3) then does not speak.
@export If I am a timber contractor deemed to be a worker under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic), how much of what the principal pays me counts as my remuneration (the Regulations take 25 per cent off where I pay for or provide materials or equipment)?
GIVEN `I am deemed a worker as a timber contractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a timber contractor deemed to be a worker under clause 6 of Schedule 1 to the Act (you fell trees, cut firewood or scrub, or clear or remove stumps or logs under a contract with a business, and do the work yourself)? (yes or no)
      `the amount payable to me` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the principal pays or must pay you under the timber contract, in dollars
      `the amount includes materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that amount include an amount for materials or equipment you need to do the work? (yes or no)
      `I purchase the materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you buy, or have you bought, materials or equipment needed to do the work? (yes or no)
      `I provide my own materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide your own materials or equipment for the work? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of my timber contract payment is my remuneration` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am deemed a worker as a timber contractor`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the materials circumstances hold` `the amount includes materials or equipment` `I purchase the materials or equipment` `I provide my own materials or equipment`
         THEN JUST (`the amount payable to me` MINUS (`the amount payable to me` TIMES `the timber contractor percentage`))
         ELSE JUST `the amount payable to me`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 11 and Schedule 2 — contractors: amounts that are not remuneration (2013 Act Sch 1 cl 9(5)(c))`
-- Situation: this group only arises if you are an individual deemed to be a worker under clause 9 (a contractor
-- who provides at least 80 per cent of the services personally).
-- cl 9(5)(c): the total amount paid or payable by the principal to the contractor, less (i) the applicable
-- prescribed percentage (if any), or (ii) if there is none, the part of that amount not attributable to the
-- provision of labour, is deemed to be remuneration.

DECLARE `Contract for services of` IS ONE OF
    `architects`
    `draftspersons`
    `engineers`
    `bricklayers`
    `building supervisors`
    `carpenters`
    `carpet layers`
    `computer programmers`
    `driving instructors`
    `fencing contractors`
    `painters`
    `resilient floor layers`
    `roof tilers or slaters`
    `plasterers`
    `cabinet makers`
    `electricians`
    `plumbers`
    `wall and floor tilers`
    `blind fitters`
    `another kind of service`

-- Column 2 of the Table in Schedule 2 to the Regulations. Building supervisors only "who provide their own vehicles
-- and are required to supervise and inspect more than 6 different building sites each 7-day period"; driving
-- instructors only "who provide their own vehicles". A contract the Table does not name has no prescribed percentage.
GIVEN `the contract` IS A `Contract for services of`,
      `own vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sites each 7 days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the Schedule 2 percentage for` `the contract` `own vehicle` `sites each 7 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the contract`
    WHEN `architects`              THEN JUST (5%)
    WHEN `draftspersons`           THEN JUST (5%)
    WHEN `engineers`               THEN JUST (5%)
    WHEN `bricklayers`             THEN JUST (30%)
    WHEN `building supervisors`    THEN IF `own vehicle` AND `sites each 7 days` GREATER THAN 6
                                        THEN JUST (25%)
                                        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `carpenters`              THEN JUST (25%)
    WHEN `carpet layers`           THEN JUST (25%)
    WHEN `computer programmers`    THEN JUST (5%)
    WHEN `driving instructors`     THEN IF `own vehicle` THEN JUST (30%) ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `fencing contractors`     THEN JUST (25%)
    WHEN `painters`                THEN JUST (15%)
    WHEN `resilient floor layers`  THEN JUST (37%)
    WHEN `roof tilers or slaters`  THEN JUST (25%)
    WHEN `plasterers`              THEN JUST (20%)
    WHEN `cabinet makers`          THEN JUST (30%)
    WHEN `electricians`            THEN JUST (25%)
    WHEN `plumbers`                THEN JUST (25%)
    WHEN `wall and floor tilers`   THEN JUST (25%)
    WHEN `blind fitters`           THEN JUST (25%)
    WHEN `another kind of service` THEN NOTHING

-- reg 11(1): the percentage applies only "in the circumstances set out in subregulation (2)".
GIVEN `the contract` IS A `Contract for services of`,
      `own vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sites each 7 days` IS A NUMBER,
      `includes materials` IS A BOOLEAN, `purchases materials` IS A BOOLEAN, `provides own materials` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the applicable prescribed percentage for` `the contract` `own vehicle` `sites each 7 days` `includes materials` `purchases materials` `provides own materials` MEANS
    IF `the materials circumstances hold` `includes materials` `purchases materials` `provides own materials`
    THEN `the Schedule 2 percentage for` `the contract` `own vehicle` `sites each 7 days`
    ELSE NOTHING

@export If I am a contractor deemed to be a worker under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic), what percentage of my contract payments do the Regulations take off as not remuneration? (No answer means no percentage is prescribed for me.)
GIVEN `my contract is for services of` IS A `Contract for services of` @desc The kind of services your contract is for, as named in Schedule 2 to the Regulations; "another kind of service" if it is not named there
      `I provide my own vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide your own vehicle for the work? (yes or no; matters only for building supervisors and driving instructors)
      `building sites I supervise each 7 days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many different building sites you are required to supervise and inspect each 7-day period (matters only for building supervisors; 0 otherwise)
      `the payments include materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the amounts paid or payable under your contract include an amount for materials or equipment needed to provide the services? (yes or no)
      `I purchase the materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you buy, or have you bought, materials or equipment needed to provide the services? (yes or no)
      `I provide my own materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide your own materials or equipment for the services? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What percentage of my contract payments is not remuneration` MEANS
    `the applicable prescribed percentage for` `my contract is for services of` `I provide my own vehicle` `building sites I supervise each 7 days` `the payments include materials or equipment` `I purchase the materials or equipment` `I provide my own materials or equipment`

@export If I am a contractor deemed to be a worker under clause 9 of Schedule 1 to the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic), how much of what the principal pays me counts as my remuneration?
GIVEN `I am deemed a worker as a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you deemed to be a worker under clause 9 of Schedule 1 to the Act (you provide at least 80 per cent of the contract's services yourself, and the Authority has not found you carry on an independent business)? (yes or no)
      `the total amount payable to me` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount the principal pays or must pay under the contract for the relevant period, in dollars
      `my contract is for services of` IS A `Contract for services of` @desc The kind of services your contract is for, as named in Schedule 2 to the Regulations; "another kind of service" if it is not named there
      `I provide my own vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide your own vehicle for the work? (yes or no; matters only for building supervisors and driving instructors)
      `building sites I supervise each 7 days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many different building sites you are required to supervise and inspect each 7-day period (matters only for building supervisors; 0 otherwise)
      `the payments include materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the amounts paid or payable under your contract include an amount for materials or equipment needed to provide the services? (yes or no)
      `I purchase the materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you buy, or have you bought, materials or equipment needed to provide the services? (yes or no)
      `I provide my own materials or equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide your own materials or equipment for the services? (yes or no)
      `the part not attributable to labour` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of the total amount that is not for your labour, in dollars (used only where no percentage is prescribed for you)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of my contract payment is my remuneration` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I am deemed a worker as a contractor`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the percentage`
         WHEN JUST `p` THEN JUST (`the total amount payable to me` MINUS (`the total amount payable to me` TIMES `p`))
         WHEN NOTHING  THEN JUST (`the total amount payable to me` MINUS `the part not attributable to labour`)
    WHERE
        `the percentage` MEANS
            `the applicable prescribed percentage for` `my contract is for services of` `I provide my own vehicle` `building sites I supervise each 7 days` `the payments include materials or equipment` `I purchase the materials or equipment` `I provide my own materials or equipment`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 12 — weekly payments to a worker living outside Australia (2013 Act s 175(4))`
-- Situation: this group only arises if you live outside Australia and receive weekly payments.
-- s 175(4): a worker who does not reside in Australia and is receiving weekly payments because of s 175(1), (2) or
-- (2A) "is entitled to receive the weekly payments if the worker proves in the prescribed manner and at the
-- prescribed intervals to the satisfaction of the Authority or self-insurer (a) the worker's identity; and (b) that
-- the worker continues to have no current work capacity".
-- reg 12(2): the manner (four steps); reg 12(4): "intervals of 3 months".

`the prescribed interval in months` MEANS 3

DECLARE `Overseas party` IS ONE OF `the worker living overseas`

-- The action carries the three things that must be done before submitting (reg 12(2)(a)-(c)).
DECLARE `Overseas action` IS ONE OF
    `submits the statement and certificate` HAS
        `statement of identity completed on the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
        `examined by a medical practitioner`                    IS A BOOLEAN
        `certificate completed on the approved form`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- The duty for one interval: within the interval (counted in days), submit to the Authority or self-insurer a
-- completed statement and certificate, made in the prescribed manner (reg 12(2)(d)). Missing it leaves the worker
-- not entitled under s 175(4) (the BREACH stands for that: the Act states no penalty).
GIVEN `the interval in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Overseas party` `Overseas action`
`the proof of identity and incapacity for one interval` `the interval in days` MEANS
    PARTY `the worker living overseas`
    MUST `submits the statement and certificate` `statement done` `examined` `certificate done` PROVIDED `statement done` AND `examined` AND `certificate done`
    WITHIN `the interval in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the worker living overseas` BECAUSE "identity and continuing incapacity not proved in the prescribed manner within the 3-month interval (s 175(4), reg 12)"

GIVEN `I do not reside in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid because of s 175` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 175(4) applies to` `I do not reside in Australia` `paid because of s 175` MEANS
    `I do not reside in Australia` AND `paid because of s 175`

@export Must I prove my identity and my continuing lack of work capacity every 3 months to keep receiving weekly payments while I live outside Australia, under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) and its Regulations?
GIVEN `I do not live in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live (reside) outside Australia? (yes or no)
      `I receive weekly payments under section 175` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving weekly payments because the Authority or self-insurer was satisfied under section 175(1), (2) or (2A) (that you have no current work capacity, likely indefinitely)? (yes or no)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I prove my identity and incapacity every 3 months` MEANS
    `section 175(4) applies to` `I do not live in Australia` `I receive weekly payments under section 175`

@export What must I do to prove my identity and continuing lack of work capacity while I live outside Australia, under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2024 (Vic)? (An empty list means the requirement does not apply to me.)
GIVEN `I do not live in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live (reside) outside Australia? (yes or no)
      `I receive weekly payments under section 175` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving weekly payments because the Authority or self-insurer was satisfied under section 175(1), (2) or (2A)? (yes or no)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`What must I do to prove my identity and incapacity` MEANS
    IF `section 175(4) applies to` `I do not live in Australia` `I receive weekly payments under section 175`
    THEN LIST
        "Complete a statement of identity in the form approved by the Authority (reg 12(2)(a)); the Authority publishes its approved forms on its website (reg 12(3))."
        "Submit to an examination by a medical practitioner (reg 12(2)(b))."
        "Obtain from the medical practitioner a certificate completed in the form approved by the Authority (reg 12(2)(c))."
        "Submit the completed statement and the completed certificate to the Authority or self-insurer (reg 12(2)(d))."
        "Do this at intervals of 3 months (reg 12(4))."
    ELSE EMPTY

@export By what date must I next prove my identity and continuing lack of work capacity while I live outside Australia, under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2024 (Vic)? (No answer means the requirement does not apply to me.)
GIVEN `I do not live in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live (reside) outside Australia? (yes or no)
      `I receive weekly payments under section 175` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving weekly payments because the Authority or self-insurer was satisfied under section 175(1), (2) or (2A)? (yes or no)
      `the date my current interval began` IS A DATE @desc The date you last submitted your statement and certificate, or, if you have not yet, the date your weekly payments while living overseas began
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I next prove my identity and incapacity` MEANS
    IF `section 175(4) applies to` `I do not live in Australia` `I receive weekly payments under section 175`
    THEN JUST (`the date months after` `the date my current interval began` `the prescribed interval in months`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Built on the duty above: the plain facts become one event on the duty's timeline.
-- NOTHING where s 175(4) does not apply (s 175(1), (2), (2A) then govern, not encoded here); JUST FALSE where it
-- applies and its "if" fails.
@export Am I entitled to receive my weekly payments for this 3-month interval while I live outside Australia, under section 175(4) of the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) and regulation 12?
GIVEN `I do not live in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live (reside) outside Australia? (yes or no)
      `I receive weekly payments under section 175` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving weekly payments because the Authority or self-insurer was satisfied under section 175(1), (2) or (2A)? (yes or no)
      `the date my current interval began` IS A DATE @desc The date you last submitted your statement and certificate, or, if you have not yet, the date your weekly payments while living overseas began
      `I completed the statement of identity on the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you complete a statement of identity in the form approved by the Authority? (yes or no)
      `a medical practitioner examined me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you submit to an examination by a medical practitioner? (yes or no)
      `I got the certificate on the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get from that medical practitioner a certificate completed in the form approved by the Authority? (yes or no)
      `I submitted the statement and certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you submitted the completed statement and certificate to the Authority or self-insurer for this interval? (yes or no)
      `the date I submitted them` IS A DATE @desc The date you submitted them (ignored if you have not)
      `the Authority or self-insurer is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority or self-insurer satisfied by what you submitted of your identity and that you still have no current work capacity? (yes or no; a decision for them, not you)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to my weekly payments for this interval while overseas` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`section 175(4) applies to` `I do not live in Australia` `I receive weekly payments under section 175`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`proved in time` AND `the Authority or self-insurer is satisfied`)
    WHERE
        `the interval in days` MEANS
            `days from` `the date my current interval began` `to` (`the date months after` `the date my current interval began` `the prescribed interval in months`)
        `the submission events` MEANS
            IF `I submitted the statement and certificate`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the worker living overseas` (`submits the statement and certificate` `I completed the statement of identity on the approved form` `a medical practitioner examined me` `I got the certificate on the approved form`) (`the day number of` `the date I submitted them`))
            ELSE EMPTY
        `proved in time` MEANS
            IF `I submitted the statement and certificate`
               AND `falls on or before` `the date my current interval began` `the date I submitted them`
            THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the proof of identity and incapacity for one interval` `the interval in days`) (`the day number of` `the date my current interval began`) `the submission events`
                 WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
                 OTHERWISE FALSE
            ELSE FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 6 — inquiries and investigations into fraud (2013 Act s 586)`
-- Situation: this group only arises if the Authority is inquiring into or investigating your activities under
-- s 586.

@export If the Victorian WorkCover Authority is inquiring into or investigating my activities for suspected fraud under section 586 of the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic), how must it conduct the inquiry? (An empty list means the regulation does not apply.)
GIVEN `the Authority is inquiring into my activities under section 586` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority inquiring into or investigating activities of yours under section 586 of the Act (suspected offences such as fraud)? (yes or no)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`How must an inquiry into me be conducted` MEANS
    IF `the Authority is inquiring into my activities under section 586`
    THEN LIST
        "With due care (reg 6(a))."
        "Objectively (reg 6(b))."
        "With regard for your legal rights as a person whose activities are being inquired into or investigated (reg 6(c))."
    ELSE EMPTY
